IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `dfa-fences`

-- Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) -- the questions people ask, for three seats in one layer (the Q&A layer).
--
-- ROLES. The seat is a parameter: every exported question takes `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"). The
-- baseline's one seat, the neighbouring owner, is two people with different questions, and the Act adds a third:
--   - the owner who wants a dividing fence built or repaired (gives the notices, builds, claims half);
--   - the owner whose neighbour wants them to share the cost (receives the notices and claims, may be made to pay);
--   - the tenant of land the fence borders: s 19 divides an owner's contribution between landlord and tenant, and a
--     tenant with 5 or more years left is an owner (s 5).
-- A question about another role answers `does not arise for you` without reading any other input. The Magistrates
-- Court is never a seat: what it may do appears as what the person may apply for, and when.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the graffiti encoding). Within a role, a question that arises only in a situation takes that
-- situation's fact straight after `my role` and answers `does not arise for you` when it does not hold, reading nothing
-- else. The questions of one situation share one input, character for character, across the two owner roles:
--   - `a notice to fence has been given between my neighbour and me` (both owners): s 9 (applying to the court) and
--     s 10 (building the whole fence after an agreement or order on a notice) arise only after a s 8 notice. FALSE gives
--     does not arise; the baseline's `a notice to fence was given by me or to me` is TRUE by it;
--   - `my neighbour has claimed half the value of a fence they built` (the owner asked to pay): s 13(3), (4), (7).
--     FALSE gives does not arise;
--   - `my land is let to a tenant` (both owners): the landlord's part of the contribution (s 19). FALSE gives does not
--     arise.
-- A question that arises in every situation of its role takes no situation input.
--
-- CONTENT. Every exported question of the baseline (dfa-fences.l4) is asked by calling its function: for the owner who
-- wants the fence, all but s 19's tenant question, which goes to the tenant. For the owner asked to pay, the same rules
-- are asked from the other side: the notice received, the neighbour's s 10 and s 15 rights against me (the s 15 answer
-- turned round by helpers that list every value), and the s 21 entry onto my land. Added from the text: the landlord's
-- part (s 19(1)) and the tenant's recovery or set-off of an excess (s 19(2)).
--
-- No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input. Edition, scope and findings: NOTES.md.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I own land and want a dividing fence built or repaired`
    `I own land and my neighbour wants me to share the cost of a dividing fence`
    `I rent land that a dividing fence borders`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Fraction` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `a fraction of the cost` HAS `fraction` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `New fence share` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `my share` HAS `share of a new fence` IS A `My share of a new fence`

DECLARE `Fence claim` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `my claim` HAS `claim for a fence I built` IS A `My claim for a fence I built`

DECLARE `Claim against me` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `where I stand` HAS `where I stand on a claim` IS A `Where I stand on a claim for half`

DECLARE `Repair recovery` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `I can recover` HAS `what I can recover` IS A `What I can recover for a repair`

-- The s 15 answer from the side of the owner the repair cost is claimed from.
DECLARE `What my neighbour can recover from me for a repair` IS ONE OF
    `half: my neighbour may repair at once without notice and recover half from me (s 15(7)(b))`
    `the whole: my neighbour may repair and recover the whole cost from me, as I have not repaired damage I am bound to repair (s 15(8))`
    `nothing yet: I am bound to repair it myself as soon as practicable (s 15(7)(c))`
    `nothing: my neighbour is bound to repair it as soon as practicable (s 15(7)(c))`
    `half: I did not reply within 14 days, so my neighbour may repair and recover half from me (s 15(7))`
    `each of us bears the cost of repairing the part we built (s 15(7)(a))`
    `half, in the way I chose from the repair notice (ss 14, 15(3)(a))`
    `the Magistrates Court decides, if my neighbour applies under s 15(4)`
    `nothing yet: my neighbour must give me a repair notice and wait 14 days for my written reply (s 15(1), (3))`

DECLARE `Repair claim against me` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `my neighbour can recover` HAS `what my neighbour can recover` IS A `What my neighbour can recover from me for a repair`

DECLARE `My reply to a repair notice` IS ONE OF
    `I have not replied in writing`
    `I agreed in writing to join in one of the ways the notice offered`
    `I disputed the need or objected to the repairs, in writing`

§§ `Turning the s 15 rule round (helpers)`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

-- The cause, as the owner asked to pay states it ("my neglect" is theirs), turned into the baseline's frame (where "my"
-- is the owner repairing). Each helper lists every value with no OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31).
GIVEN `the cause` IS A `How the fence came to need repair`
GIVETH A `How the fence came to need repair`
`the cause from the other side` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the cause`
    WHEN `wear, age or ordinary deterioration` THEN `wear, age or ordinary deterioration`
    WHEN `flood, fire, lightning, storm, tempest or accident, through nobody's neglect` THEN `flood, fire, lightning, storm, tempest or accident, through nobody's neglect`
    WHEN `a fire or a falling tree through my neighbour's neglect` THEN `a fire or a falling tree through my neglect`
    WHEN `a fire or a falling tree through my neglect` THEN `a fire or a falling tree through my neighbour's neglect`

GIVEN `my reply` IS A `My reply to a repair notice`
GIVETH A `Reply to my repair notice`
`the reply as the baseline states it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my reply`
    WHEN `I have not replied in writing` THEN `no written reply`
    WHEN `I agreed in writing to join in one of the ways the notice offered` THEN `agrees in writing to join in one of the ways I offered`
    WHEN `I disputed the need or objected to the repairs, in writing` THEN `disputes the need or objects to the repairs, in writing`

GIVEN `the answer` IS A `What I can recover for a repair`
GIVETH A `What my neighbour can recover from me for a repair`
`the answer from the other side` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `half: I may repair at once without notice and recover half (s 15(7)(b))` THEN `half: my neighbour may repair at once without notice and recover half from me (s 15(7)(b))`
    WHEN `the whole: I may repair and recover the whole cost from my neighbour (s 15(8))` THEN `the whole: my neighbour may repair and recover the whole cost from me, as I have not repaired damage I am bound to repair (s 15(8))`
    WHEN `nothing yet: my neighbour is bound to repair it as soon as practicable (s 15(7)(c))` THEN `nothing yet: I am bound to repair it myself as soon as practicable (s 15(7)(c))`
    WHEN `nothing: I am bound to repair it myself as soon as practicable (s 15(7)(c))` THEN `nothing: my neighbour is bound to repair it as soon as practicable (s 15(7)(c))`
    WHEN `half: my neighbour did not reply within 14 days, so I may repair and recover half (s 15(7))` THEN `half: I did not reply within 14 days, so my neighbour may repair and recover half from me (s 15(7))`
    WHEN `each of us bears the cost of repairing the part we built (s 15(7)(a))` THEN `each of us bears the cost of repairing the part we built (s 15(7)(a))`
    WHEN `half, in the way my neighbour chose from my notice (ss 14, 15(3)(a))` THEN `half, in the way I chose from the repair notice (ss 14, 15(3)(a))`
    WHEN `the Magistrates Court decides: I may apply under s 15(4)` THEN `the Magistrates Court decides, if my neighbour applies under s 15(4)`
    WHEN `nothing yet: I must give a repair notice and wait 14 days for a written reply (s 15(1), (3))` THEN `nothing yet: my neighbour must give me a repair notice and wait 14 days for my written reply (s 15(1), (3))`

-- The baseline's s 15 answer for the neighbour who repairs, from the facts as the owner asked to pay states them.
GIVEN `the cause` IS A `How the fence came to need repair`
      `each of us built part of the fence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my neighbour gave me a repair notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days since I received the repair notice` IS A NUMBER
      `my reply` IS A `My reply to a repair notice`
      `I have failed to repair damage I am bound to repair` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What I can recover for a repair`
`the repairing neighbour's answer` MEANS
    `What can I recover for repairing the fence` (`the cause from the other side` `the cause`) `each of us built part of the fence` `my neighbour gave me a repair notice` `days since I received the repair notice` (`the reply as the baseline states it` `my reply`) `I have failed to repair damage I am bound to repair`

§§ `For the owner who wants a dividing fence built or repaired`

§§§ `Who is an owner, and what fence (s 5)`

@export Am I an owner of the land for the Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) s 5?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my interest` IS A `My interest in the land` @desc What interest you have in the land
      `years left on my lease` IS A NUMBER @desc If you hold a lease: the unexpired term in years when the fencing or repair notice is given (0 otherwise)
      `the land is vested in me as a public reserve or park` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold the land as trustee of a public reserve, public park or other prescribed public purpose
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I an owner, wanting the fence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land and want a dividing fence built or repaired` THEN
        `yes if` (`Am I an owner under the Act` `my interest` `years left on my lease` `the land is vested in me as a public reserve or park`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is our dividing fence a sufficient fence under the Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) s 5?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a local law prescribes a sufficient fence for our area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the local government's local law prescribes a sufficient fence for the part of the district where the fence is or will be
      `the fence is of a kind the local law prescribes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fence is one the local law prescribes as sufficient
      `my neighbour and I agreed its description and quality` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your neighbour agreed on the description and quality of the fence
      `the fence is of the kind we agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fence matches what you agreed
      `the agreed fence fails to comply with the local law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreed fence fails to comply with the local law (FALSE if there is no local law)
      `the fence is substantial and ordinarily resists cattle and sheep` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fence is substantial and ordinarily capable of resisting the trespass of cattle and sheep
      `the court has determined it sufficient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Magistrates Court has determined it to be a sufficient fence
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the fence sufficient, wanting the fence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land and want a dividing fence built or repaired` THEN
        `yes if` (`Is the fence a sufficient fence` `a local law prescribes a sufficient fence for our area` `the fence is of a kind the local law prescribes` `my neighbour and I agreed its description and quality` `the fence is of the kind we agreed` `the agreed fence fails to comply with the local law` `the fence is substantial and ordinarily resists cattle and sheep` `the court has determined it sufficient`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `A new fence (ss 4, 6-10, 22)`

@export What share of a new dividing fence must I bear (Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) ss 4, 6, 7)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am an owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an owner under s 5 (freehold, entitled to the rents, or a lease with 5 or more years left)
      `my neighbour is an owner bound by the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your neighbour is an owner under s 5 and not the Crown (s 4)
      `our lands adjoin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your land and your neighbour's land adjoin
      `our lands are divided by a sufficient fence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a sufficient fence (s 5) already divides the two lands
      `we have an agreement about the cost` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your neighbour have a covenant, contract or agreement about the cost of the fence
GIVETH A `New fence share`
`What is my share of a new fence, wanting the fence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land and want a dividing fence built or repaired` THEN
        `my share` (`What share of a new dividing fence must I bear` `I am an owner` `my neighbour is an owner bound by the Act` `our lands adjoin` `our lands are divided by a sufficient fence` `we have an agreement about the cost`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much must I contribute to a new dividing fence under s 7, where there is no agreement about the cost?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the cost of the fence` IS A NUMBER @desc The cost of constructing the dividing fence, in dollars
      `I am an owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an owner under s 5 (freehold, entitled to the rents, or a lease with 5 or more years left)
      `my neighbour is an owner bound by the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your neighbour is an owner under s 5 and not the Crown (s 4)
      `our lands adjoin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your land and your neighbour's land adjoin
      `our lands are divided by a sufficient fence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a sufficient fence (s 5) already divides the two lands
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much must I contribute, wanting the fence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land and want a dividing fence built or repaired` THEN
        amount (`How much must I contribute to the new fence` `the cost of the fence` `I am an owner` `my neighbour is an owner bound by the Act` `our lands adjoin` `our lands are divided by a sufficient fence`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my notice to fence a valid notice under the Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) ss 8 and 22?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `it is in writing and signed by the owner giving it or their attorney or agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice is written and signed by the owner giving it, or by their attorney or agent
      `it specifies the boundary, or the other line where the boundary is impracticable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it names the boundary to be fenced (or another line, if the land makes the boundary impracticable)
      `it contains a proposal for fencing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it contains a proposal for fencing that boundary or line
      `it specifies the kind of fence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it states the kind of fence proposed
      `it was delivered personally or sent by registered mail` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was handed to the owner receiving it personally or sent by registered mail to their usual or last known home (for a company: left at or posted to its principal office in WA)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my notice to fence valid, wanting the fence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land and want a dividing fence built or repaired` THEN
        `yes if` (`Is my notice to fence valid` `it is in writing and signed by the owner giving it or their attorney or agent` `it specifies the boundary, or the other line where the boundary is impracticable` `it contains a proposal for fencing` `it specifies the kind of fence` `it was delivered personally or sent by registered mail`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I apply to the Magistrates Court to settle the new dividing fence (Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) s 9)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a notice to fence has been given between my neighbour and me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a valid s 8 notice to fence has been given, by you to your neighbour or by your neighbour to you
      `days since the notice was given` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days have passed since the notice was given
      `we agree on the need, the line and the kind of fence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your neighbour agree on all of: the need for the fence, where it goes, and what kind it is
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I apply to the court, wanting the fence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land and want a dividing fence built or repaired` THEN
        IF NOT `a notice to fence has been given between my neighbour and me`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May I apply to the Magistrates Court about the new fence` TRUE `days since the notice was given` `we agree on the need, the line and the kind of fence`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I build the whole fence myself and recover half the cost from my neighbour (Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) s 10)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a notice to fence has been given between my neighbour and me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a valid s 8 notice to fence has been given, by you to your neighbour or by your neighbour to you
      `we agreed the fence or the court ordered it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your neighbour agreed the fence after the notice to fence, or the court made an order under s 9
      `my neighbour has done their part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your neighbour has performed their part of the agreement or order
      `months named in the agreement or order` IS A NUMBER @desc The time the agreement or order gives to build, in months (0 if it names no time)
      `months since the agreement or order` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months have passed since the date of the agreement or order
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I build the whole fence, wanting the fence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land and want a dividing fence built or repaired` THEN
        IF NOT `a notice to fence has been given between my neighbour and me`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May I build the whole fence and recover half` `we agreed the fence or the court ordered it` `my neighbour has done their part` `months named in the agreement or order` `months since the agreement or order`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I make my neighbour pay half the value of a fence I built without giving notice (Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) s 13)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the fence is a sufficient fence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fence you built is a sufficient fence (s 5)
      `I gave a notice to fence before building` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave a s 8 notice to fence before you built
      `my neighbour has built on, occupies or lets a building on their land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your neighbour has completed a substantial building or structure on their land, occupies one there, or lets someone lawfully occupy one
      `I have already received half the value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or the land's previous owner) have already been paid half the value of the fence
GIVETH A `Fence claim`
`Can I claim half the value of my fence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land and want a dividing fence built or repaired` THEN
        `my claim` (`Can I claim half the value of the fence I built` `the fence is a sufficient fence` `I gave a notice to fence before building` `my neighbour has built on, occupies or lets a building on their land` `I have already received half the value`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Repairs and entry (ss 14, 15, 21)`

@export What can I recover from my neighbour for repairing our dividing fence (Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) ss 14, 15)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the cause` IS A `How the fence came to need repair` @desc How the fence came to need repair ("my" is you, "my neighbour" the other owner)
      `each of us built part of the fence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fence was built partly by you and partly by your neighbour
      `I gave a repair notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave your neighbour a written s 15 notice requiring them to assist in repairing the fence
      `days since my neighbour received it` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days have passed since your neighbour received the repair notice (0 if none given)
      `the reply` IS A `Reply to my repair notice` @desc What your neighbour replied in writing to your repair notice
      `my neighbour has failed to repair damage they are bound to repair` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Where the damage came from your neighbour's neglect: whether they have failed to repair or renew the fence
GIVETH A `Repair recovery`
`What can I recover for a repair, wanting the fence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land and want a dividing fence built or repaired` THEN
        `I can recover` (`What can I recover for repairing the fence` `the cause` `each of us built part of the fence` `I gave a repair notice` `days since my neighbour received it` `the reply` `my neighbour has failed to repair damage they are bound to repair`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much of the repair cost can I recover, given the answer to what I can recover (Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) s 15)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the answer` IS A `What I can recover for a repair` @desc The answer to "What can I recover for repairing the fence"
      `the cost of the repair` IS A NUMBER @desc What the repair cost, in dollars
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much of the repair can I recover, wanting the fence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land and want a dividing fence built or repaired` THEN
        amount (`How much of the repair cost can I recover` `the answer` `the cost of the repair`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I go onto my neighbour's land to build or repair the dividing fence (Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) s 21)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the fence is being built or repaired under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fence is being constructed or repaired under the Act (by you or your neighbour, or an agent or contractor)
      `it is a reasonable time during the work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a reasonable time during the construction or repair
      `what is done there is necessary or reasonably required for the work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what would be done on the adjoining land is necessary or reasonably required to build or repair the fence
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I enter my neighbour's land` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land and want a dividing fence built or repaired` THEN
        `yes if` (`May I enter my neighbour's land for the fence work` `the fence is being built or repaired under the Act` `it is a reasonable time during the work` `what is done there is necessary or reasonably required for the work`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `If my land is let (s 19)`

-- s 19(1): as between landlord and tenant, the landlord pays the whole for a tenant's term under 5 years, three-fourths
-- for 5 to under 7, one-half for 7 to under 12, nothing for 12 or more: one less the tenant's part, which the baseline
-- works out.
@export My land is let: what fraction of the contribution to a dividing fence do I bear as landlord, as against my tenant, absent an agreement (Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) s 19)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my land is let to a tenant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land on your side of the fence is held by a tenant of yours
      `the term of the tenancy in years` IS A NUMBER @desc The term of the tenant's interest, in years, at the time the fence is built or repaired
GIVETH A `Fraction`
`What fraction do I bear as landlord, wanting the fence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land and want a dividing fence built or repaired` THEN
        IF NOT `my land is let to a tenant`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `a fraction of the cost` (1 MINUS `What fraction of the fence cost do I bear as tenant` `the term of the tenancy in years`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the owner whose neighbour wants them to share the cost`

§§§ `Who is an owner, and what fence (s 5)`

@export Am I an owner of the land for the Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) s 5, so that I can be made to share the cost?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my interest` IS A `My interest in the land` @desc What interest you have in the land
      `years left on my lease` IS A NUMBER @desc If you hold a lease: the unexpired term in years when the fencing or repair notice is given (0 otherwise)
      `the land is vested in me as a public reserve or park` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold the land as trustee of a public reserve, public park or other prescribed public purpose
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I an owner, asked to pay` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land and my neighbour wants me to share the cost of a dividing fence` THEN
        `yes if` (`Am I an owner under the Act` `my interest` `years left on my lease` `the land is vested in me as a public reserve or park`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is our dividing fence a sufficient fence under the Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) s 5, as the owner asked to share its cost?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a local law prescribes a sufficient fence for our area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the local government's local law prescribes a sufficient fence for the part of the district where the fence is or will be
      `the fence is of a kind the local law prescribes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fence is one the local law prescribes as sufficient
      `my neighbour and I agreed its description and quality` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your neighbour agreed on the description and quality of the fence
      `the fence is of the kind we agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fence matches what you agreed
      `the agreed fence fails to comply with the local law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreed fence fails to comply with the local law (FALSE if there is no local law)
      `the fence is substantial and ordinarily resists cattle and sheep` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fence is substantial and ordinarily capable of resisting the trespass of cattle and sheep
      `the court has determined it sufficient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Magistrates Court has determined it to be a sufficient fence
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the fence sufficient, asked to pay` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land and my neighbour wants me to share the cost of a dividing fence` THEN
        `yes if` (`Is the fence a sufficient fence` `a local law prescribes a sufficient fence for our area` `the fence is of a kind the local law prescribes` `my neighbour and I agreed its description and quality` `the fence is of the kind we agreed` `the agreed fence fails to comply with the local law` `the fence is substantial and ordinarily resists cattle and sheep` `the court has determined it sufficient`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `A new fence (ss 4, 6-10, 13, 22)`

@export My neighbour wants a new dividing fence: what share of it must I bear (Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) ss 4, 6, 7)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am an owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an owner under s 5 (freehold, entitled to the rents, or a lease with 5 or more years left)
      `my neighbour is an owner bound by the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your neighbour is an owner under s 5 and not the Crown (s 4)
      `our lands adjoin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your land and your neighbour's land adjoin
      `our lands are divided by a sufficient fence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a sufficient fence (s 5) already divides the two lands
      `we have an agreement about the cost` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your neighbour have a covenant, contract or agreement about the cost of the fence
GIVETH A `New fence share`
`What is my share of a new fence, asked to pay` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land and my neighbour wants me to share the cost of a dividing fence` THEN
        `my share` (`What share of a new dividing fence must I bear` `I am an owner` `my neighbour is an owner bound by the Act` `our lands adjoin` `our lands are divided by a sufficient fence` `we have an agreement about the cost`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export My neighbour wants a new dividing fence: how much must I contribute under s 7, where there is no agreement about the cost?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the cost of the fence` IS A NUMBER @desc The cost of constructing the dividing fence, in dollars
      `I am an owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an owner under s 5 (freehold, entitled to the rents, or a lease with 5 or more years left)
      `my neighbour is an owner bound by the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your neighbour is an owner under s 5 and not the Crown (s 4)
      `our lands adjoin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your land and your neighbour's land adjoin
      `our lands are divided by a sufficient fence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a sufficient fence (s 5) already divides the two lands
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much must I contribute, asked to pay` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land and my neighbour wants me to share the cost of a dividing fence` THEN
        amount (`How much must I contribute to the new fence` `the cost of the fence` `I am an owner` `my neighbour is an owner bound by the Act` `our lands adjoin` `our lands are divided by a sufficient fence`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is the notice to fence I received a valid notice under the Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) ss 8 and 22?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `it is in writing and signed by the owner giving it or their attorney or agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice is written and signed by the owner giving it, or by their attorney or agent
      `it specifies the boundary, or the other line where the boundary is impracticable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it names the boundary to be fenced (or another line, if the land makes the boundary impracticable)
      `it contains a proposal for fencing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it contains a proposal for fencing that boundary or line
      `it specifies the kind of fence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it states the kind of fence proposed
      `it was delivered personally or sent by registered mail` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was handed to the owner receiving it personally or sent by registered mail to their usual or last known home (for a company: left at or posted to its principal office in WA)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the notice I received valid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land and my neighbour wants me to share the cost of a dividing fence` THEN
        `yes if` (`Is my notice to fence valid` `it is in writing and signed by the owner giving it or their attorney or agent` `it specifies the boundary, or the other line where the boundary is impracticable` `it contains a proposal for fencing` `it specifies the kind of fence` `it was delivered personally or sent by registered mail`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 9(1): the court may decide "on an application by either of those owners".
@export May I apply to the Magistrates Court to settle the dividing fence my neighbour wants (Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) s 9)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a notice to fence has been given between my neighbour and me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a valid s 8 notice to fence has been given, by you to your neighbour or by your neighbour to you
      `days since the notice was given` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days have passed since the notice was given
      `we agree on the need, the line and the kind of fence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your neighbour agree on all of: the need for the fence, where it goes, and what kind it is
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I apply to the court, asked to pay` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land and my neighbour wants me to share the cost of a dividing fence` THEN
        IF NOT `a notice to fence has been given between my neighbour and me`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May I apply to the Magistrates Court about the new fence` TRUE `days since the notice was given` `we agree on the need, the line and the kind of fence`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 10: if "either of those owners fails" within the time, "the other of those owners may construct the whole fence"
-- and recover half. The baseline's function, asked of my neighbour with my part as the part not done.
@export Can my neighbour build the whole fence and recover half the cost from me (Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) s 10)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a notice to fence has been given between my neighbour and me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a valid s 8 notice to fence has been given, by you to your neighbour or by your neighbour to you
      `we agreed the fence or the court ordered it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your neighbour agreed the fence after the notice to fence, or the court made an order under s 9
      `I have done my part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have performed your part of the agreement or order
      `months named in the agreement or order` IS A NUMBER @desc The time the agreement or order gives to build, in months (0 if it names no time)
      `months since the agreement or order` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months have passed since the date of the agreement or order
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can my neighbour build the whole fence and recover half from me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land and my neighbour wants me to share the cost of a dividing fence` THEN
        IF NOT `a notice to fence has been given between my neighbour and me`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May I build the whole fence and recover half` `we agreed the fence or the court ordered it` `I have done my part` `months named in the agreement or order` `months since the agreement or order`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export I have received a claim for half the value of a fence my neighbour built: must I pay it (Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) s 13(3), (4), (7))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my neighbour has claimed half the value of a fence they built` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your neighbour has given you a notice claiming half the value of a dividing fence they built without a notice to fence (s 13(2))
      `I have paid it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have paid the amount of the claim
      `I gave written notice disputing it within one month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, within one month of receiving the claim, you gave written notice that you dispute it
      `a month has passed since I received it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether one month has passed since you received the claim
GIVETH A `Claim against me`
`Must I pay the claim for half` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land and my neighbour wants me to share the cost of a dividing fence` THEN
        IF NOT `my neighbour has claimed half the value of a fence they built`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `where I stand` (`Must I pay my neighbour's claim for half` `I have paid it` `I gave written notice disputing it within one month` `a month has passed since I received it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Repairs and entry (ss 14, 15, 21)`

@export What can my neighbour recover from me for repairing our dividing fence (Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) ss 14, 15)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the cause` IS A `How the fence came to need repair` @desc How the fence came to need repair ("my" is you, "my neighbour" the other owner)
      `each of us built part of the fence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fence was built partly by you and partly by your neighbour
      `my neighbour gave me a repair notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your neighbour gave you a written s 15 notice requiring you to assist in repairing the fence
      `days since I received the repair notice` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days have passed since you received the repair notice (0 if none)
      `my reply` IS A `My reply to a repair notice` @desc What you replied in writing to the repair notice
      `I have failed to repair damage I am bound to repair` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Where the damage came from your neglect: whether you have failed to repair or renew the fence
GIVETH A `Repair claim against me`
`What can my neighbour recover from me for a repair` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land and my neighbour wants me to share the cost of a dividing fence` THEN
        `my neighbour can recover` (`the answer from the other side` (`the repairing neighbour's answer` `the cause` `each of us built part of the fence` `my neighbour gave me a repair notice` `days since I received the repair notice` `my reply` `I have failed to repair damage I am bound to repair`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much of the repair cost can my neighbour recover from me, in dollars (Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) s 15)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the cause` IS A `How the fence came to need repair` @desc How the fence came to need repair ("my" is you, "my neighbour" the other owner)
      `each of us built part of the fence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fence was built partly by you and partly by your neighbour
      `my neighbour gave me a repair notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your neighbour gave you a written s 15 notice requiring you to assist in repairing the fence
      `days since I received the repair notice` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days have passed since you received the repair notice (0 if none)
      `my reply` IS A `My reply to a repair notice` @desc What you replied in writing to the repair notice
      `I have failed to repair damage I am bound to repair` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Where the damage came from your neglect: whether you have failed to repair or renew the fence
      `the cost of the repair` IS A NUMBER @desc What the repair cost, in dollars
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much of the repair can my neighbour recover from me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land and my neighbour wants me to share the cost of a dividing fence` THEN
        amount (`How much of the repair cost can I recover` (`the repairing neighbour's answer` `the cause` `each of us built part of the fence` `my neighbour gave me a repair notice` `days since I received the repair notice` `my reply` `I have failed to repair damage I am bound to repair`) `the cost of the repair`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May my neighbour come onto my land to build or repair the dividing fence (Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) s 21)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the fence is being built or repaired under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fence is being constructed or repaired under the Act (by you or your neighbour, or an agent or contractor)
      `it is a reasonable time during the work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a reasonable time during the construction or repair
      `what is done there is necessary or reasonably required for the work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what would be done on the adjoining land is necessary or reasonably required to build or repair the fence
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May my neighbour come onto my land` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land and my neighbour wants me to share the cost of a dividing fence` THEN
        `yes if` (`May I enter my neighbour's land for the fence work` `the fence is being built or repaired under the Act` `it is a reasonable time during the work` `what is done there is necessary or reasonably required for the work`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `If my land is let (s 19)`

@export My land is let: what fraction of my contribution to the dividing fence do I bear as landlord, as against my tenant, absent an agreement (Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) s 19)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my land is let to a tenant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land on your side of the fence is held by a tenant of yours
      `the term of the tenancy in years` IS A NUMBER @desc The term of the tenant's interest, in years, at the time the fence is built or repaired
GIVETH A `Fraction`
`What fraction do I bear as landlord, asked to pay` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own land and my neighbour wants me to share the cost of a dividing fence` THEN
        IF NOT `my land is let to a tenant`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `a fraction of the cost` (1 MINUS `What fraction of the fence cost do I bear as tenant` `the term of the tenancy in years`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the tenant of land a dividing fence borders`

-- s 5 "owner" (b): a lessee is an owner if the unexpired term is 5 years or more. The baseline's function, with the
-- lease as the interest.
@export Am I, as a tenant, treated as an owner who can be made to share the cost of a dividing fence (Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) s 5)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `years left on my lease` IS A NUMBER @desc If you hold a lease: the unexpired term in years when the fencing or repair notice is given (0 otherwise)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I an owner, as a tenant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I rent land that a dividing fence borders` THEN
        `yes if` (`Am I an owner under the Act` `I hold a lease` `years left on my lease` FALSE)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export As a tenant, what fraction of the contribution to a dividing fence must I bear as against my landlord, absent an agreement (Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) s 19)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the term of my lease in years` IS A NUMBER @desc The term of your tenancy, in years, at the time the fence is built or repaired
GIVETH A `Fraction`
`What fraction do I bear as tenant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I rent land that a dividing fence borders` THEN
        `a fraction of the cost` (`What fraction of the fence cost do I bear as tenant` `the term of my lease in years`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 19(2): "Where either the landlord or the tenant pays a greater proportion of the cost than he is required to pay
-- under this section, he may recover ... the excess from his tenant or landlord, and any tenant may set off any sum
-- recoverable by him under this section against any rent payable to his landlord."
@export If I paid more than my share as against my landlord, can I recover the excess, or set it off against my rent (Dividing Fences Act 1961 (WA) s 19(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I paid more than my share under s 19` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you paid a greater part of the fence cost than s 19 (or your agreement with the landlord) requires of you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I recover the excess from my landlord` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I rent land that a dividing fence borders` THEN `yes if` `I paid more than my share under s 19`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
